{"id":"dea0e944a5a296c9","group":"58","path":"58/batch13/58-thm-reflection.md","title":"Reflection Principle","display":"thm-reflection — Reflection Principle","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-reflection","aliases":["58-thm-reflection","Reflection Principle","Montague-Levy Reflection"],"display":"thm-reflection — Reflection Principle","depends_on":["[[../batch09/58-df-reflection-principle.md]]","[[../batch12/58-df-v-alpha.md]]","[[../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-reflection"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-reflection</span><span>Reflection Principle</span><span>Montague-Levy Reflection</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-reflection — Reflection Principle"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"6994aafd3bf766a5\" href=\"?note=6994aafd3bf766a5\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-reflection-principle.md\">../batch09/58-df-reflection-principle.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"aabdf3005231e9dc\" href=\"?note=aabdf3005231e9dc\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-v-alpha.md\">../batch12/58-df-v-alpha.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"5582a281f15a33c2\" href=\"?note=5582a281f15a33c2\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md\">../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi_1(\\vec x,p),\\ldots,\\varphi_n(\\vec x,p)\">\\(\\varphi_1(\\vec x,p),\\ldots,\\varphi_n(\\vec x,p)\\)</span> (a fixed finite metalinguistic family of set-theory formulas)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p \\in V\">\\(p \\in V\\)</span> (set parameter)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Ord}\">\\(\\mathrm{Ord}\\)</span> (class of ordinals)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}reflection}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\forall p\\in V\\;\\forall\\gamma\\in\\mathrm{Ord}\\;\n\\exists\\beta\\in\\mathrm{Ord}\\;\n\\left[\n\\gamma&lt;\\beta\n\\land p\\in V_\\beta\n\\land\n\\bigwedge_{i=1}^{n}\\;\n\\forall\\vec a\\in V_\\beta^{&lt;\\omega}\\;\n\\left(\n\\varphi_i(\\vec a,p)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\varphi_i^{V_\\beta}(\\vec a,p)\n\\right)\n\\right]\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}reflection}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\forall p\\in V\\;\\forall\\gamma\\in\\mathrm{Ord}\\;\n\\exists\\beta\\in\\mathrm{Ord}\\;\n\\left[\n\\gamma&lt;\\beta\n\\land p\\in V_\\beta\n\\land\n\\bigwedge_{i=1}^{n}\\;\n\\forall\\vec a\\in V_\\beta^{&lt;\\omega}\\;\n\\left(\n\\varphi_i(\\vec a,p)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\varphi_i^{V_\\beta}(\\vec a,p)\n\\right)\n\\right]\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Montague (1961), Levy: reflection principle.</li>\n<li>Only the displayed finite family of formulas is reflected; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V_\\beta\\prec V\">\\(V_\\beta\\prec V\\)</span> for all formulas would contradict standard limitations.</li>\n<li>The parameter condition <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p\\in V_\\beta\">\\(p\\in V_\\beta\\)</span> is required for the relativized satisfaction statements to be typed.</li>\n<li>The reflecting ordinals are unbounded; the formulation above records this using the arbitrary lower bound <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\gamma\">\\(\\gamma\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>This is explicitly a metatheoretic finite-formula schema.  It does not quantify over a truth predicate for the proper class <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V\">\\(V\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch09/58-df-reflection-principle.md","status":"resolved","id":"6994aafd3bf766a5","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch09/58-df-reflection-principle.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch12/58-df-v-alpha.md","status":"resolved","id":"aabdf3005231e9dc","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-df-v-alpha.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md","status":"resolved","id":"5582a281f15a33c2","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\varphi_1(\\vec x,p),\\ldots,\\varphi_n(\\vec x,p)","display":false},{"tex":"p \\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Ord}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}reflection}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\forall p\\in V\\;\\forall\\gamma\\in\\mathrm{Ord}\\;\n\\exists\\beta\\in\\mathrm{Ord}\\;\n\\left[\n\\gamma<\\beta\n\\land p\\in V_\\beta\n\\land\n\\bigwedge_{i=1}^{n}\\;\n\\forall\\vec a\\in V_\\beta^{<\\omega}\\;\n\\left(\n\\varphi_i(\\vec a,p)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\varphi_i^{V_\\beta}(\\vec a,p)\n\\right)\n\\right]","display":true},{"tex":"V_\\beta\\prec V","display":false},{"tex":"p\\in V_\\beta","display":false},{"tex":"\\gamma","display":false},{"tex":"V","display":false}],"bytes":1512,"backlinks":[{"id":"3a899ab7d4901585","anchor":"ref-1","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"5232bfe264029cd2","anchor":"ref-2","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"ebaf7fe36df3a088","anchor":"ref-1","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4391","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"